# PORTFOLIO_OS — Cursor Rules
# Cybersecurity Portfolio · Next.js 14+ · TypeScript · Tailwind · Framer Motion · Zustand

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 1 — PROJECT IDENTITY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

You are an expert Next.js 14 engineer, TypeScript architect, and UI/UX specialist
building a cybersecurity-themed developer portfolio. The aesthetic is a dark terminal
OS — think Matrix green on black, system log cards, and a CLI-driven navigation layer.

The owner is a cybersecurity student and full-stack developer. Every technical decision
should reflect the standards expected of a security-conscious engineer. Code quality,
security hygiene, and accessibility are not optional — they are part of the brand.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 2 — TECHNICAL STACK (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Framework:     Next.js 14+ with App Router only. Never use Pages Router patterns.
Language:      TypeScript in strict mode. Zero tolerance for `any` or implicit types.
Styling:       Tailwind CSS using the custom token set defined in tailwind.config.ts.
               Never use inline style attributes unless driven by a dynamic JS value
               that cannot be expressed as a Tailwind class (e.g. a CSS custom property
               updated by a mousemove listener).
Animation:     Framer Motion for layout animations, accordions, and scroll-triggered
               effects. CSS keyframes (defined in globals.css) for ambient loops like
               the CRT flicker and typing cursor.
State:         Zustand exclusively for global state. React useState for local UI state
               that does not need to be shared. Never use useContext for state that
               changes frequently — it causes unnecessary re-renders.
Icons:         Lucide React for generic UI icons. Local SVGs from
               /public/assets/tools/ for tool-specific logos (Wireshark, Nmap, etc.).
Testing:       Vitest for unit and component tests. Playwright for E2E tests.
Deployment:    Vercel with all security headers configured in next.config.js.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 3 — DESIGN SYSTEM TOKENS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Always use these token names from tailwind.config.ts. Never hardcode hex values
directly in component files.

Backgrounds:
  void          #000000    Main page background
  component     #0D0D0D    Sidebar, card backgrounds
  card-hover    #121212    Card hover state

Accents:
  matrix-green  #00FF41    Primary accent — CLI, sidebar border, default glow
  cyber-orange  #FF5F00    Warning / CRIT / KERNEL log channel
  app-cyan      #00CCFF    APP_DEV log channel
  warn-yellow   #FFD700    SYS_ADMIN log channel

Typography:
  font-mono: JetBrains Mono → Fira Code → system monospace fallback

Log channel to colour mapping (use these consistently everywhere):
  KERNEL    → cyber-orange
  SEC_OPS   → matrix-green
  APP_DEV   → app-cyan
  SYS_ADMIN → warn-yellow

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 4 — FILE STRUCTURE RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Respect the established directory structure. Never create files outside these paths
without a clear architectural reason documented in a comment.

  src/app/                  Next.js App Router routes and special files
  src/components/layout/    Global persistent UI (CliHeader, Sidebar, MobileFab, ErrorBoundary)
  src/components/sections/  One file per page section (HeroSection, ProjectsSection, etc.)
  src/components/ui/        Reusable leaf components (ProjectLogCard, CertBadge, etc.)
  src/data/                 registry.ts and constants.ts — the only source of truth for content
  src/hooks/                Custom React hooks (useScrollSpy, useCommandEngine)
  src/store/                Zustand store (useSystemStore.ts — one file, all slices)
  src/types/                index.ts — all shared TypeScript interfaces
  src/utils/                Pure utility functions (commandEngine, hexDump, sanitise)
  public/assets/fonts/      Self-hosted font files only
  public/assets/tools/      SVG icons for development tools
  public/assets/certs/      Certification badge images
  tests/unit/               Vitest unit and component tests
  tests/e2e/                Playwright end-to-end tests

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 5 — TYPESCRIPT RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- Strict mode is always on. Never disable it or add @ts-ignore.
- Never use `any`. If you are tempted to use `any`, define a proper interface instead.
- Never use non-null assertion (`!`) unless you have verified the value cannot be null
  at that point in the code and left a comment explaining why.
- All props interfaces must be defined and named, not inlined as object literals.
- Union types for constrained string values (LogChannel, LogLevel, CertStatus, etc.)
  are already defined in src/types/index.ts. Always import and use them — never
  re-declare them or use plain `string` where a union is available.
- Use `satisfies` operator when validating that a data literal matches an interface
  without widening the type, especially in registry.ts.
- Export only what needs to be consumed outside the file. Keep helpers private.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 6 — COMPONENT RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- Every section component (HeroSection, ProjectsSection, etc.) must be wrapped in
  its own ErrorBoundary instance in page.tsx. A crash in one section must not
  affect any other section.
- Every component file that uses browser APIs (window, document, IntersectionObserver)
  must guard with `typeof window !== 'undefined'` or use the `'use client'` directive.
- Server Components are preferred by default. Only add `'use client'` when the
  component uses hooks, event handlers, or browser APIs.
- Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML anywhere in this project. All CLI output is
  rendered as plain text nodes only.
- All links to external URLs must include `rel="noopener noreferrer"` and
  `target="_blank"`.
- The resume path must always be read from `src/data/constants.ts` — never
  hardcoded in a component.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 7 — STATE MANAGEMENT RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- The Zustand store (useSystemStore.ts) is the single source of truth for:
    activeSection, sidebarExpanded, sidebarMobileOpen, cliInput, cliHistory,
    activeProjectId, cleanModeEnabled, glitchActive.
- Local useState is acceptable for ephemeral UI state that no other component
  needs to know about (e.g. whether a dropdown inside a card is open).
- Never derive state by reading the DOM (e.g. checking scroll position directly
  in a component). Use the useScrollSpy hook which manages IntersectionObserver
  and writes to Zustand.
- All entries pushed to cliHistory must pass through the sanitiseCLIOutput
  function from src/utils/sanitise.ts before being stored. This is enforced by
  always using the pushCliHistory store action, never writing to cliHistory directly.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 8 — ANIMATION RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- Every animation must have a prefers-reduced-motion fallback. This is not optional.
  The global override in globals.css handles ambient CSS keyframes automatically.
  For Framer Motion animations, use the useReducedMotion() hook and pass a
  no-motion variant when it returns true.
- Never animate properties that trigger layout (width, height, top, left, margin,
  padding). Animate only transform and opacity. For accordion height animations,
  use Framer Motion's layout prop which uses transforms internally.
- The CRT scanline overlay div and the flicker keyframe on the root body are both
  conditionally active based on cleanModeEnabled in Zustand. When cleanModeEnabled
  is true, the overlay must be unmounted from the DOM entirely — not hidden with
  display:none or visibility:hidden.
- The skills section scan line fires once per page load when the section first
  enters the viewport. It must not re-fire on subsequent scrolls. Disconnect the
  IntersectionObserver after the first trigger.
- Framer Motion AnimatePresence must wrap any component that conditionally renders,
  including accordion content, the mobile sidebar overlay, and the glitch overlay.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 9 — ACCESSIBILITY RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- Target WCAG AA compliance as a minimum across the entire application.
- All interactive elements must have visible focus styles. Use a matrix-green
  outline (outline: 2px solid #00FF41, outline-offset: 2px) as the global
  focus style in globals.css.
- The CLI header input must not trap keyboard focus. Tab from the input must
  move focus to the first focusable element in the sidebar.
- The mobile sidebar overlay must trap focus while open. Use the inert attribute
  on the main content or a focus trap utility.
- All icon-only buttons (the clean mode eye icon, the mobile FAB) must have
  aria-label attributes. Lucide React icons inside buttons need aria-hidden="true".
- Toggle buttons must use aria-pressed reflecting the current state.
- Expandable cards (ProjectLogCard, CertBadge verbose mode) must use aria-expanded
  on the toggle element.
- The certification progress bar must use role="progressbar" with aria-valuenow,
  aria-valuemin, aria-valuemax, and aria-label.
- Skill badge grid items must carry aria-label stating the skill name and
  proficiency level as a fraction (e.g. "Wireshark, proficiency 4 of 5").
- Images loaded with next/image must always have a meaningful alt attribute.
  Decorative images use alt="".

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 10 — SECURITY RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

This is a cybersecurity portfolio. The code itself is part of the portfolio.
Security mistakes here are a red flag to the exact audience you are trying to impress.

- Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML. This rule is repeated from Section 6 because
  it is the most critical XSS vector in React.
- All CLI command output must pass through sanitiseCLIOutput before being stored
  or rendered. This is not negotiable.
- All security headers (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, etc.) are configured in
  next.config.js. Never remove or loosen them without a documented reason.
- External resources (fonts, icons) are self-hosted in /public/assets/. Do not
  add external CDN dependencies that would require loosening the CSP.
- The Content Security Policy must remain strict. If a new feature requires
  relaxing the CSP, document exactly why in next.config.js with a comment.
- Never commit real credentials, tokens, or personal contact details to the
  repository. Use environment variables for anything sensitive and document
  them in .env.example.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 11 — DATA LAYER RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- src/data/registry.ts is the single source of truth for all content.
  Components never hardcode content — they always read from the registry.
- src/data/constants.ts is the single source of truth for all URLs, paths,
  and configuration values referenced in more than one place.
- The hidden boolean flag on Project and IntelEntry controls production
  visibility. Setting hidden: true excludes the entry from all renders without
  deleting it from the codebase.
- The sidebar directory tree is generated dynamically from the registry.
  Never hardcode sidebar entries in the Sidebar component. If a new logChannel
  is added to the data, the sidebar must reflect it automatically.
- When adding a new project to the registry, all required fields must be
  populated. Optional fields (githubUrl, liveUrl, vulnType) may be omitted
  but must not be left as empty strings — use undefined instead.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 12 — TESTING RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- The sanitiser utility must have unit tests written before it is used anywhere
  in the application. Tests first, integration second.
- Every utility function in src/utils/ must have a corresponding test file
  in tests/unit/.
- Component tests must verify the null-render behaviour of CertBadge when
  status is 'planned'. This is a safety net for the most common content mistake.
- E2E tests must cover: boot sequence completion, CLI navigation commands,
  accordion single-expansion behaviour, resume link target, and the 404 page.
- Do not mock the Zustand store in component tests. Use the real store with
  a reset call in beforeEach to ensure test isolation.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 13 — PERFORMANCE RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- Target: initial JS bundle under 150 KB gzipped, LCP under 2.5 s on 4G,
  CLS under 0.1.
- Framer Motion must not be included in the initial bundle. Import it only
  in client components that actually use it. Use next/dynamic with ssr: false
  for heavy animated sections if the Lighthouse score drops below 90.
- All images use next/image with explicit width and height to prevent CLS.
- Fonts are self-hosted with font-display: optional to eliminate FOUT and CLS.
- The IntersectionObserver in useScrollSpy creates one observer instance for
  all sections — never one observer per section.
- The skills section scan line observer must disconnect after its first trigger
  to avoid unnecessary callback invocations on subsequent scrolls.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 14 — CODE STYLE AND DOCUMENTATION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

- All exported functions in src/utils/ and src/hooks/ must have JSDoc comments
  with @param, @returns, and @example.
- Component files do not need JSDoc on the component function itself, but
  complex internal helpers within a component file should have a one-line comment.
- Use named exports everywhere. Default exports are only used for Next.js
  special files (page.tsx, layout.tsx, not-found.tsx, etc.) where the framework
  requires them.
- Imports must be ordered: React and Next.js imports first, then third-party
  libraries, then internal absolute imports, then relative imports. Separate
  each group with a blank line.
- No commented-out code in committed files. Use the hidden flag in the registry
  to disable content, and use feature branches to disable features.
- Variable and function names use camelCase. Type and interface names use
  PascalCase. Constants that are truly constant (never reassigned) use
  SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE only when they represent a fixed configuration value
  (e.g. MAX_CLI_HISTORY_LENGTH). Tailwind class strings are exempt.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION 15 — WHAT NOT TO DO
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Never do any of the following:

- Use the Pages Router. This project uses App Router exclusively.
- Use `any` in TypeScript.
- Use dangerouslySetInnerHTML anywhere.
- Hardcode hex colour values in component files — use Tailwind tokens.
- Hardcode the resume path, GitHub URL, LinkedIn URL, or email address
  anywhere other than src/data/constants.ts.
- Add external CDN links for fonts or icons — all assets are self-hosted.
- Create one IntersectionObserver per section in the scroll-spy hook.
- Allow the skills section scan animation to re-fire on repeated scrolls.
- Render a CertBadge with status 'planned' — the component returns null.
- Push unsanitised strings to the CLI history array.
- Use display:none to hide the CRT overlay when clean mode is active —
  unmount it from the DOM.
- Loosen the Content Security Policy without a documented justification.
- Commit .env files. Only .env.example is committed.
- Skip the prefers-reduced-motion fallback on any animation.


# Additional Snippets:

- Be extremely concise. Do not explain code unless asked. Skip apologies. If modifying a file, only show the changed blocks unless a full rewrite is safer.

